Never commit actual secrets. Validate environment variables during application startup and display a useful setup error when required configuration is missing.

Do not hardcode project credentials.

### Dependency rules

Inspect the existing repository before installing packages. Reuse compatible dependencies, avoid unnecessary replacements, and pin compatible versions in the lockfile.

Do not create a separate backend framework merely for appearance. Implement each operation using an appropriate secure Supabase mechanism. If an Express API is genuinely needed, keep it separate from browser code and document its setup and deployment.

